---
import type { calculateIndex } from "../index.ts";
import { samplePeriod } from "../lib/presentation.ts";
interface Props {
  index: ReturnType<typeof calculateIndex>;
}
const { index } = Astro.props;
---

<details id="method" class="about">
  <summary>About the index</summary>
  <p>
    This is a joke, not a forecast. The Fireship Index measures AI coverage in
    recent videos from{" "}
    <a
      href="https://www.youtube.com/@Fireship"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Fireship
    </a>
    . It does not measure job losses or the chance of human extinction. This
    project is independent and is not affiliated with Fireship.
  </p>
  <p>
    Titles and descriptions are checked for AI terms and model names. Sponsor
    calls to action, course links, and repeated channel text are excluded where
    possible. Each matching video lists its terms and their source. These rules
    can miss context.
  </p>
  <p>
    The latest 15 available uploads count, regardless of age. A shorter feed
    uses its available count. Score = 100 × (0.6 × AI share + 0.4 × min(AI
    uploads per week ÷ 3, 1)), rounded. AI share is matched uploads ÷ sampled
    uploads. The sample period starts at the oldest included upload and ends at
    the calculation time, with a minimum of one day. An empty sample has no
    score.
  </p>
  <p id="sample-period">{samplePeriod(index)}</p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare fetches the original RSS feed from YouTube. The page and{" "}
    <a href="/api/feed">feed API</a> use the same saved data. Cached results are
    checked for renewal after 15 minutes when requested. The last valid feed is
    kept during an outage. The check time is shown above. No external relay or
    AI model is used.
  </p>
  <details class="import-panel">
    <summary>Import the original RSS file</summary>
    <p>
      You can also save{" "}
      <a
        href="https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UCsBjURrPoezykLs9EqgamOA"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Fireship’s RSS feed
      </a>{" "}
      as XML and select it below. This local preview stays in your browser and
      does not change the public index.
    </p>
    <label for="feed-file">Fireship RSS file</label>
    <input
      id="feed-file"
      type="file"
      accept=".xml,.rss,.atom,text/xml,application/xml,application/atom+xml"
    />
    <p id="import-status" role="status"></p>
  </details>
</details>
